From: macbook-pro-T1 contributors
Subject: [PATCH] brcmfmac: report selected PCIe board-data filename and length

Report successful optional NVRAM loading without dumping calibration or device
identity. This distinguishes an actual board-data download from binary fallback.

SPDX-License-Identifier: ISC
--- a/brcmfmac/pcie.c
+++ b/brcmfmac/pcie.c
@@ -1720,6 +1720,8 @@
 	brcmf_pcie_write_ram32(devinfo, devinfo->ci->ramsize - 4, 0);
 
 	if (nvram) {
+		dev_info(&devinfo->pdev->dev, "board data %s (%u bytes)\n",
+			   devinfo->nvram_name, nvram_len);
 		brcmf_dbg(PCIE, "Download NVRAM %s\n", devinfo->nvram_name);
 		address = devinfo->ci->rambase + devinfo->ci->ramsize -
 			  nvram_len;
